  "body": "Found in M5's review of #573 (#557).\n\n**Today:** arming a part-axis pick (+X/+Y by Edge or Two points) or a lay-on-plane face/points pick on the Setups page, then switching to another page (e.g. an operation's properties) leaves the pick armed. Edge/vertex/face clicks on the part there feed the hidden Setups draft instead of the open operation's geometry pick.\n\n**Expected:** leaving the Setups page (or closing the section) disarms every Setups pick; clicks then go to the page that is shown. Re-opening the page shows the picks disarmed (the draft's picked items kept).\n\n**Done means:** a headless test arms each pick, switches to an operation page, clicks an edge/vertex/face, and the operation's geometry (not the setup draft) receives it; returning shows the picks disarmed.",
